   ```c
   ret = btrfs_inode_by_name(dir, dentry, &location, &di_type);
   if (ret < 0)
       return ERR_PTR(ret);
   ```
   This function call retrieves the inode information based on the directory and dentry. If an error occurs, it returns an error pointer. This is a basic error handling mechanism but does not explicitly check the integrity of the retrieved data structure.

3. **Checking Inode Type**:
   ```c
   if (location.type == BTRFS_INODE_ITEM_KEY) {
       inode = btrfs_iget(dir->i_sb, &location, root, NULL);
       if (IS_ERR(inode))
           return inode;

       /* Do extra check against inode mode with di_type */
