The code snippet uses `kzalloc` to allocate and zero-initialize the structure, ensuring that all fields, including pointers, start at a known state (zero). Additionally, pointers are explicitly set to point to valid locations or copied from other structures. There is no indication that any pointers are left uninitialized or pointing to stale memory.

